<!--
  THE ANSWER: one property, in <properties>, in exercise/pom.xml.

  maven-jar-plugin (and maven-assembly-plugin, and maven-shade-plugin, and every other
  archiver Maven ships) reads project.build.outputTimestamp. When it is absent, each zip
  entry is stamped with the wall clock at the moment it was written, so two builds of
  byte-identical class files produce two different files. When it is present, every entry
  gets THIS instant instead and the jar becomes a function of its inputs.

  The value is an ISO-8601 instant in UTC, or a Unix epoch in seconds. A real project sets
  it from the commit it is building - `git log -1 --format=%cI` - so the jar is a function
  of the source, which is the whole idea.
-->
<project.build.outputTimestamp>2026-09-15T00:00:00Z</project.build.outputTimestamp>
